# Confirms an A/B trial boot. Started ONLY by novadeck-boot-good.path -- hence no [Install].
#
# THE SIGNAL is gamescope's startup handshake, plus the session still being alive 30s later.
#
# Reaching that handshake proves, in one shot: drm/msm bound and took DRM master, the panel
# modeset, mesa initialised, both nested Xwaylands came up, libseat got an active seat through
# logind, and SDDM's PAM autologin worked. It is the earliest instant at which "the screen is
# showing something" is actually true. The weaker candidates all mark a black screen good:
# graphical.target reached only proves sddm.service was STARTED, and an active logind session is
# the same problem one layer up. The stricter one -- waiting for SteamUI -- would roll back a
# healthy OS over an OOBE, an offline first boot, or a Steam-side outage.
#
# The 30s re-check is not padding. sddm.conf.d autologin sets Relogin=true, so a session that
# dies immediately is restarted forever; without the delay a boot stuck in that loop would mark
# itself good on its first iteration. --require-marker re-tests the marker after the sleep, and
# novadeck-session's EXIT trap removes it, so "still there" means "the same session stayed up".
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO TIMEOUT THAT MARKS GOOD ANYWAY. If the session never comes up, the
# path unit never fires, pending stays set, and the next boot rolls back. That is the property
# this whole mechanism exists for; a backstop timer would defeat it.
#
# Known gap: gamescope up with Steam wedged shows a blank compositor and still confirms. Pass 2
# tightens it -- novadeck-steamos-manager touches a second marker on SteamUI's first D-Bus call.
[Unit]
Description=novadeck confirm this A/B trial boot (session came up and stayed up)
Documentation=file:///usr/bin/novadeck-bootctl
ConditionPathExists=/run/novadeck/boot

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/sleep 30
ExecStart=/usr/bin/novadeck-bootctl mark-good --require-marker
